WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.392
A CTE has a simple structure.

00:00:02.392 --> 00:00:05.232
WITH gives the stage a name.

00:00:05.232 --> 00:00:10.302
The query inside the parentheses defines the rows and columns of that stage.

00:00:10.302 --> 00:00:13.687
The final query can read the CTE by name.

00:00:13.687 --> 00:00:17.937
You can also define several CTEs separated by commas.

00:00:17.937 --> 00:00:20.512
The CTE is not a permanent table.

00:00:20.512 --> 00:00:22.457
It belongs to the statement.

00:00:22.457 --> 00:00:29.132
A CTE gives a name to an intermediate result so a complex query can be read in stages.

00:00:29.132 --> 00:00:36.882
Use it to clarify grain changes and major transformations, not simply to break every two lines into a

00:00:36.882 --> 00:00:44.878
new block. A useful CTE name describes what the rows represent, such as patient_totals or ranked_visits.
